From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 08:16:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] msxml3: Answer attribute lookups and types as each MSXML
 version does.

Excel reads the uri of each <ext> element in an .xlsx with
getValueFromName(NULL, 0, L"uri", 3); when that fails it drops the
extension and calls the workbook damaged.  Measured on Windows 11 with
the attributes a reader hands to startElement:

- MSXML 6 takes a missing namespace with a zero length as none; MSXML 3
  answers E_INVALIDARG for a missing namespace or local name, and
  E_POINTER only for a missing index.
- MSXML 6 clears every output first, the index to 0 and strings to NULL
  and 0, whether the call succeeds or not; MSXML 3 leaves them.
- getType(), getTypeFromName() and getTypeFromQName() answer CDATA, or
  the type the DTD declares: the keyword, (a|b) for an enumeration and
  NOTATION (a|b) for a notation.
- The lookups that return a value or a type check their outputs before
  looking for the attribute.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

